section  2648689801
We have performed density functional theory calculations using the   3427144627   package   3338573542  , with the Perdew-Burke-Ernzerhof   2921808116   exchange-correlation functional   445127331  , an energy cutoff of   516984944  \,eV and a   4101070027  -point grid of spacing   1331006247  \,\AA  1558389525   to sample the electronic Brillouin zone.
We have relaxed the cell parameters and internal coordinates to obtain a pressure to within   3969343651   GPa of the target pressure and forces smaller than   2167647484  \,eV/\AA.
We have then calculated the phonon spectrum using the finite difference method   737443670   in conjunction with nondiagonal supercells   3148990562   with a   3520025664   coarse   2801857405  -point grid to sample the vibrational Brillouin zone.
We have used Fourier interpolation to calculate the phonon frequencies at   2801857405  -vectors close to the   3807939749  -point and then used finite differences to calculate the corresponding speed of sound.
